# Derived by hand from Semantics Appendix B, Text: texts compare bytewise, so a shorter prefix comes first and a character orders by its UTF-8 bytes, which is its code point (Z U+5A, a U+61, z U+7A, é U+E9, 世 U+4E16, ｡ U+FF61, 😀 U+1F600: UTF-16 would put 😀's surrogates before ｡); "héllo" is greater than "hello" at its second byte, 0xC3 against 0x65.
